    "title": "McKinstry records second four-hit game of career - NewsBreak",
    "text": "WASHINGTON, D.C. (WANE) – North Side High School graduate Zach McKinstry racked up the second four-hit game of his MLB career on Wednesday afternoon, as the Fort Wayne native went 4-for-5 in an 11-2 win by the Detroit Tigers in the first game of a split doubleheader against the Nationals. McKinstry’s other four-hit game came on Sept. 11, 2022 against the Giants when the Summit City native was playing for the Chicago Cubs. McKinstry doubled in the first inning, then followed it up with three singles to raise his batting average to .293 at the time. The Tigers lost the nightcap to the Nationals, 9-4. McKinstry went 0-for-3 in the second game, dropping his average to .290. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WANE 15.",
